    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Polymarket TriAgent × n8n — ADAPTIVE / EVENT-DRIVEN\n\n**Template only; remains INACTIVE.** No provider API keys and no ChatGPT browser scraping.\n\n1. Keep existing TriAgent collector + forensic evidence store.\n2. Build authenticated local bridge (port `8791`), assign n8n **HTTP Header Auth** credential to ALL HTTP nodes and **Header Auth** to webhook. Local `127.0.0.1` only.\n3. `work.ready`, `mission.completed` and `alert.early` trigger immediate wake. n8n launches one async job at a time per available worker. Jobs do **not** wait inside n8n.\n4. Every **15 minutes**: LOCAL recovery of PID/heartbeat/state. **No AI calls** from this timer. ETA is calculated by bridge from prior observed job durations. Collector remains its own fast process.\n5. GPT research director = official **Codex CLI** signed in with ChatGPT subscription, **not** ChatGPT web UI. Claude Code + optional authenticated Grok CLI. No paid API keys required *if these CLIs support your plans*.\n6. Mission completes → bridge saves evidence + emits event → n8n wakes → GPT audits, can queue next mission. Calibration, provenance and false-positive controls are mandatory.\n\n**Don't activate until** bridge security + idempotency + CLI auth tested and old scheduler disabled. A JSON template alone does not run autonomous agents.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 1390,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1230,
        -270
      ],
      "id": "19633823-74e0-5e75-ab92-136f58b314de",
      "name": "Read this before activation"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Local bridge endpoints and contract\n\n- `POST /v1/events/ingest`: idempotently record event_id; return `{event_id,alert_id,alert_ready}`. This also creates needed queued GPT review for completed missions.\n- `POST /v1/alerts/notify`: single, deduplicated local notification with case/evidence link, not a trading signal.\n- `POST /v1/work/lease`: atomic SQLite claim + provider concurrency/quota/priority/disk gate; return `{ready,job_id,lease_id,agent}`.\n- `POST /v1/work/dispatch`: validates lease, starts one **async child process**, returns HTTP 202 immediately. Fresh Codex/Claude session; verified Grok CLI. No double launch.\n- `POST /v1/work/reconcile`: local PID/heartbeat/deadline scan, classify unknown execution, update duration forecast, surface blocked jobs; MUST NOT trigger an AI completion or resubmit active jobs.\n- `POST /v1/work/reject`: block invalid agent job; do not silently discard.\n\nBridge sends authenticated POST to n8n local `/webhook/triagent-v2-wake` when an event is ready. The 15-min recovery is only fallback.\n\nn8n credential assignment is manual after import. Test from active n8n and localhost before enabling automatic launch.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 1350,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1230,
        1020
      ],
      "id": "efbcc9bb-e057-5e3e-bec9-c10f2c4a8f2c",
      "name": "Bridge API + dispatch semantics"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Predictive forensic alert ≠ proof of insider information\n\n**Two independent loops:** (a) Polymarket/Polygon data collector at an adaptive rate; (b) costly AI only on new evidence or completed tasks.\n\nDetector: point-in-time wallet age, funder concentration excluding bridges/exchanges, coordinated first funding and first fills, real-size and liquidity, time-to-event, graph links. Historical Iran/Venezuela/Ballon d'Or patterns become *hypotheses*, not ground-truth insider labels.\n\nNever feed **future cash-out / exchange destination** into an alert intended to fire before first trade. Use `observed_at` + `event_at`, watermark and exact chain provenance. Validate prospectively against matched non-suspect wallets, placebo windows, false alerts per 1k active wallets, lead time to first trade/event.\n\nNotify only calibrated HIGH / manually approved thresholds; uncertainty must be shown. When no verified novelty, enqueue zero followups.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 1200,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        -260
      ],
      "id": "acda9ce9-a787-539b-9b9b-dd20dfd9bd5c",
      "name": "Predictive alert semantics"
    }
